---
import "@fontsource-variable/geist";
import "@fontsource-variable/geist-mono";
const GH = "https://github.com/sjh9714/demoreel";
---

<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="utf-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1" />
    <title>demoreel — screen recording you can edit like code</title>
    <meta
      name="description"
      content="Record a web app session once, edit camera and timing as JSON, render a crisp deterministic GIF. vhs for web apps."
    />
  </head>
  <body>
    <nav>
      <span class="logo">demoreel<span class="cursor-blink">▌</span></span>
      <a href={GH} class="gh">GitHub →</a>
    </nav>

    <header>
      <div class="hero-copy">
        <p class="kicker">$ npm i -g demoreel</p>
        <h1>Stop screen-recording<br />your demos.</h1>
        <p class="lede">
          Record a real session in your web app once. demoreel captures the DOM,
          not pixels — so you can retime the boring parts, zoom the camera on
          clicks, and re-render a crisp README GIF from the same take, forever.
        </p>
        <div class="cta-row">
          <button class="copy-cmd" data-cmd="npm i -g demoreel">
            <span class="prompt">$</span> npm i -g demoreel
            <span class="copied">copied</span>
          </button>
          <a class="ghost" href={GH}>Star on GitHub</a>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="hero-term" aria-hidden="true">
        <div class="term-bar"><i></i><i></i><i></i></div>
        <pre><code><span class="c"># interact with your app once</span>
<span class="p">$</span> demoreel record http://localhost:3000
<span class="dim">saved 214 events → session.json</span>

<span class="c"># auto-draft camera zooms + cut idle time</span>
<span class="p">$</span> demoreel suggest
<span class="dim">wrote reel.json (10 keyframes, 3 retimes)</span>

<span class="c"># deterministic re-render, any size</span>
<span class="p">$</span> demoreel render -o demo.gif
<span class="ok">wrote demo.gif  1.1 MB · 8.4s · 1120px</span></code></pre>
      </div>
    </header>

    <section class="live">
      <div class="section-head">
        <h2>This demo is not a video</h2>
        <p>
          It's the recorded DOM session replaying live in your browser — the
          same data the GIF is rendered from. Drag the sliders: you're editing
          the reel in real time.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="live-grid">
        <div class="frame-wrap" id="frame-wrap">
          <iframe
            id="replay"
            src="/demo/replay.html?play"
            width="1280"
            height="800"
            title="live demoreel replay"
            loading="lazy"></iframe>
        </div>
        <div class="controls">
          <label>
            <span>camera zoom <em id="zoom-val">1.0×</em></span>
            <input id="zoom" type="range" min="0" max="2" step="0.05" value="1" />
          </label>
          <label>
            <span>playback speed <em id="speed-val">1.0×</em></span>
            <input id="speed" type="range" min="0.25" max="3" step="0.25" value="1" />
          </label>
          <label class="check">
            <input id="cursor" type="checkbox" checked />
            <span>synthetic cursor + click ripples</span>
          </label>
          <p class="note">
            Every knob here is a number in <code>reel.json</code>. Change it,
            re-render, get the exact same take with new direction.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="how">
      <div class="section-head">
        <h2>Edit a recording like code</h2>
        <p>One JSON file is the whole edit: what to speed up, where the camera looks.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="how-grid">
        <ol class="steps">
          <li>
            <b>record</b> — a real browser session, captured as DOM events via
            <a href="https://github.com/rrweb-io/rrweb">rrweb</a>. Data, not pixels.
          </li>
          <li>
            <b>edit</b> — <code>reel.json</code> declares retiming and camera
            keyframes. <code>demoreel suggest</code> drafts it for you from your
            clicks and idle gaps.
          </li>
          <li>
            <b>render</b> — headless Chrome steps the replay frame by frame
            (pure function of time), ffmpeg packs a palette-optimized GIF.
            Byte-identical on every run.
          </li>
        </ol>
        <pre class="reel"><code>{`{
  "session": "session.json",
  "retime": [
    { "from": 4200, "to": 9800, "speed": 4 },
    { "from": 12000, "to": 15000, "cut": true }
  ],
  "camera": [
    [0,    960, 540, 1.0 ],
    [1200, 960, 540, 1.0 ],   // hold wide
    [1700, 640, 380, 1.5 ],   // zoom to the click
    [3500, 640, 380, 1.5 ]    // hold
  ],
  "cursor": { "smooth": 120, "clickRipples": true }
}`}</code></pre>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="vs">
      <div class="section-head">
        <h2>When to use what</h2>
      </div>
      <table>
        <thead>
          <tr><th></th><th>reproducible</th><th>editable after the take</th><th>works on</th></tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr>
            <td><a href="https://github.com/charmbracelet/vhs">vhs</a></td>
            <td class="y">yes — scripted</td><td class="y">yes — it's a script</td><td>terminal apps</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td>screen recorders</td>
            <td class="n">no — re-shoot every change</td><td class="n">video editing only</td><td>anything</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td>Screen Studio</td>
            <td class="n">no — still a pixel recording</td><td class="p">zoom/cursor, in-app</td><td>macOS</td>
          </tr>
          <tr class="us">
            <td>demoreel</td>
            <td class="y">yes — DOM replay, deterministic</td><td class="y">yes — JSON, versionable</td><td>web apps</td>
          </tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </section>

    <section class="limits">
      <div class="section-head">
        <h2>Honest limitations</h2>
        <p>demoreel replays the DOM, so anything that never enters the DOM never renders:</p>
      </div>
      <ul>
        <li>cross-origin iframes (Stripe checkout, embedded YouTube)</li>
        <li><code>&lt;video&gt;</code> pixel content — playback events replay, the pixels don't</li>
        <li>browser-native UI: file pickers, permission prompts, select popups</li>
        <li>canvas needs <code>--canvas</code> at record time and costs session size</li>
        <li>native desktop apps — for terminals use vhs, it's excellent</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <footer>
      <span>MIT · built by <a href="https://github.com/sjh9714">@sjh9714</a></span>
      <span>the GIF in the <a href={GH}>README</a> was rendered by demoreel itself</span>
    </footer>

    <script>
      // scale the fixed 1280×800 replay to its container
      const wrap = document.getElementById("frame-wrap")!;
      const iframe = document.getElementById("replay") as HTMLIFrameElement;
      const fit = () => {
        const s = wrap.clientWidth / 1280;
        iframe.style.transform = `scale(${s})`;
        wrap.style.height = `${800 * s}px`;
      };
      new ResizeObserver(fit).observe(wrap);
      fit();

      // sliders → postMessage into the replay
      const state = { zoom: 1, speed: 1, cursor: true };
      const send = () => iframe.contentWindow?.postMessage({ demoreel: state }, "*");
      const bind = (id: string, key: "zoom" | "speed", label: string) => {
        const el = document.getElementById(id) as HTMLInputElement;
        el.addEventListener("input", () => {
          state[key] = Number(el.value);
          document.getElementById(label)!.textContent = `${Number(el.value).toFixed(2).replace(/0$/, "")}×`;
          send();
        });
      };
      bind("zoom", "zoom", "zoom-val");
      bind("speed", "speed", "speed-val");
      (document.getElementById("cursor") as HTMLInputElement).addEventListener("change", (e) => {
        state.cursor = (e.target as HTMLInputElement).checked;
        send();
      });

      // copy install command
      document.querySelector(".copy-cmd")?.addEventListener("click", async (e) => {
        const btn = e.currentTarget as HTMLElement;
        await navigator.clipboard.writeText(btn.dataset.cmd!);
        btn.classList.add("did-copy");
        setTimeout(() => btn.classList.remove("did-copy"), 1200);
      });
    </script>

    <style>
      :root {
        --bg: #101113;
        --bg-raise: #17181b;
        --line: #26282d;
        --text: #e7e8ea;
        --dim: #9a9da3;
        --accent: #58c48c;
        --accent-dim: #2e5e45;
        --mono: "Geist Mono Variable", ui-monospace, monospace;
        --sans: "Geist Variable", system-ui, sans-serif;
      }
      * { box-sizing: border-box; margin: 0; }
      body {
        background: var(--bg);
        color: var(--text);
        font-family: var(--sans);
        line-height: 1.6;
      }
      a { color: var(--accent); text-decoration: none; }
      a:hover { text-decoration: underline; }
      code { font-family: var(--mono); font-size: 0.92em; color: var(--accent); }

      nav {
        display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: center;
        max-width: 1200px; margin: 0 auto; padding: 22px 24px;
      }
      .logo { font-family: var(--mono); font-weight: 600; letter-spacing: -0.02em; }
      .cursor-blink { color: var(--accent); animation: blink 1.2s steps(1) infinite; }
      @keyframes blink { 50% { opacity: 0; } }
      .gh { font-family: var(--mono); font-size: 14px; color: var(--dim); }

      header {
        display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1.1fr 0.9fr; gap: 48px;
        max-width: 1200px; margin: 0 auto; padding: 72px 24px 96px;
        align-items: center;
      }
      .kicker { font-family: var(--mono); color: var(--accent); font-size: 14px; margin-bottom: 18px; }
      h1 {
        font-size: clamp(34px, 4.6vw, 56px);
        letter-spacing: -0.03em; line-height: 1.05; font-weight: 650;
      }
      .lede { color: var(--dim); margin-top: 20px; max-width: 52ch; }
      .cta-row { display: flex; gap: 14px; margin-top: 32px; flex-wrap: wrap; }
      .copy-cmd {
        position: relative; font-family: var(--mono); font-size: 14px;
        background: var(--bg-raise); color: var(--text);
        border: 1px solid var(--line); border-radius: 10px;
        padding: 12px 18px; cursor: pointer;
        transition: border-color 0.2s, transform 0.15s;
      }
      .copy-cmd:hover { border-color: var(--accent-dim); }
      .copy-cmd:active { transform: scale(0.98); }
      .copy-cmd .prompt { color: var(--accent); }
      .copied {
        position: absolute; inset: 0; display: grid; place-items: center;
        background: var(--bg-raise); border-radius: 10px; color: var(--accent);
        opacity: 0; pointer-events: none; transition: opacity 0.2s;
      }
      .did-copy .copied { opacity: 1; }
      .ghost {
        font-family: var(--mono); font-size: 14px; color: var(--dim);
        border: 1px solid transparent; padding: 12px 10px;
      }

      .hero-term {
        background: var(--bg-raise); border: 1px solid var(--line);
        border-radius: 14px; overflow: hidden;
        box-shadow: 0 24px 48px -24px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.6);
      }
      .term-bar { display: flex; gap: 6px; padding: 12px 14px; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line); }
      .term-bar i { width: 10px; height: 10px; border-radius: 50%; background: var(--line); }
      .hero-term pre { padding: 20px 22px; overflow-x: auto; }
      .hero-term code { font-size: 13px; line-height: 1.75; color: var(--text); }
      .hero-term .c { color: var(--dim); }
      .hero-term .p { color: var(--accent); }
      .hero-term .dim { color: var(--dim); }
      .hero-term .ok { color: var(--accent); }

      section { max-width: 1200px; margin: 0 auto; padding: 72px 24px; border-top: 1px solid var(--line); }
      .section-head { max-width: 60ch; margin-bottom: 40px; }
      h2 { font-size: 28px; letter-spacing: -0.02em; font-weight: 650; }
      .section-head p { color: var(--dim); margin-top: 10px; }

      .live-grid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 2fr 1fr; gap: 32px; align-items: start; }
      .frame-wrap {
        position: relative; overflow: hidden; border-radius: 14px;
        border: 1px solid var(--line); background: #141414;
      }
      .frame-wrap iframe {
        transform-origin: 0 0; border: 0; display: block;
        pointer-events: none; /* it's a movie, not a page */
      }
      .controls { display: grid; gap: 22px; padding-top: 6px; }
      .controls label { display: grid; gap: 8px; font-family: var(--mono); font-size: 13px; color: var(--dim); }
      .controls em { font-style: normal; color: var(--accent); float: right; }
      .controls label span { display: flex; justify-content: space-between; }
      input[type="range"] { accent-color: var(--accent); width: 100%; }
      .check { grid-template-columns: auto 1fr; align-items: center; }
      .note { font-size: 13px; color: var(--dim); border-left: 2px solid var(--accent-dim); padding-left: 12px; }

      .how-grid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 1.2fr; gap: 40px; align-items: start; }
      .steps { list-style: none; counter-reset: step; display: grid; gap: 24px; padding: 0; }
      .steps li { counter-increment: step; padding-left: 48px; position: relative; color: var(--dim); }
      .steps li b { color: var(--text); font-family: var(--mono); }
      .steps li::before {
        content: counter(step, decimal-leading-zero);
        position: absolute; left: 0; top: 2px;
        font-family: var(--mono); font-size: 13px; color: var(--accent);
      }
      .reel {
        background: var(--bg-raise); border: 1px solid var(--line); border-radius: 14px;
        padding: 20px 22px; overflow-x: auto;
      }
      .reel code { color: var(--text); font-size: 13px; line-height: 1.7; }

      .vs table { width: 100%; border-collapse: collapse; font-size: 14.5px; }
      .vs th { text-align: left; font-family: var(--mono); font-weight: 500; color: var(--dim); font-size: 13px; padding: 10px 14px; }
      .vs td { padding: 14px; border-top: 1px solid var(--line); }
      .vs td:first-child { font-family: var(--mono); }
      .vs .y { color: var(--accent); }
      .vs .n { color: var(--dim); }
      .vs .p { color: var(--text); }
      .vs .us { background: var(--bg-raise); }

      .limits ul { color: var(--dim); display: grid; gap: 10px; padding-left: 20px; max-width: 62ch; }

      footer {
        display: flex; justify-content: space-between; gap: 16px; flex-wrap: wrap;
        max-width: 1200px; margin: 0 auto; padding: 40px 24px 56px;
        border-top: 1px solid var(--line);
        font-family: var(--mono); font-size: 13px; color: var(--dim);
      }

      @media (max-width: 880px) {
        header, .live-grid, .how-grid { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
        header { padding-top: 40px; }
        .vs { overflow-x: auto; }
      }
    </style>
  </body>
</html>
